e>Promoter hypermethylation of multiple genes in sputum precedes lung cancer incidence in a high-risk cohort</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><volume>66</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>3338</fpage><lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16540689</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-bmi-2007-307"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bird</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>DNA methylation patterns and epigenetic memory</article-title><source>Genes Dev</source><volume>16</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>6</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11782440</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-bmi-2007-307"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Braakhuis</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tabor</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kummer</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Leemans</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Brakenhoff</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>A genetic explanation of Slaughter&#x02019;s concept of field cancerization: evidence and clinical implications</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><volume>63</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>1727</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12702551</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-bmi-2007-307"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brena</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Plass</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Quantitative assessment of DNA methylation: Potential applications for disease diagnosis, classification, and prognosis